{"id":"u-741bdb1f-59ac-4a98-ad49-1f5b8afb24f5","src":"community","title":"99 Problems but a Bench Ain't One","author":"Joseph R.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/qGMx3z-99-problems-but-a-bench-aint-one","desc":"Bench focused program with a mix of Conjugate and % based training. For intermediate to advanced lifters. % recommended is a guide, not a rule. Listen to your body. If you need to go a little lighter or heavier, that is fine. Try to stay within 7 lbs of the recommended % if you can. Note that the third day of each week it has the last set as 100%. The goal on this day is to use the Max Effort Method, not a true 1rm. All sets leading up to the 100% are basically to prime you for your \"max effort set\" which may or may not actually be 100%,  but is 100% of what you feel appropriate and safe for that day. Also note that the exercise labeled as \"Smith Machine\" is not actually Smith machine. Please use a barbell for this, I just needed a way to differentiate this bench press from the Day 1 bench press within the app. 3 days weekly, If you need more workout days, add them accordingly to your needs. Do legs or conditioning on any extra days you add. Save your arms/chest for the bench days! Just be smart about it. On my off days I do martial arts, ruck, hike, play hacky sack, trail run, or do walking lunges for 200 to 400 yards. Get creative, or add a massive leg day if you prefer. Test your 1RM's before starting and at end of the 5 weeks, then do the program again! Run the program twice before moving to something new.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-14T13:53:49.061Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"pct":65,"x":4}]},{"n":"Pin Press Bench (Barbell)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"pct":65},{"amrap":1,"pct":70},{"amrap":1,"pct":80,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}],"note":"Neutral grip plate machine"},{"n":"Neutral Grip Dumbbell Bench Press","sets":[{"amrap":1,"pct":80,"x":2},{"amrap":1,"pct":100},{"amrap":1,"pct":80}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Straight Arm Pulldown","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Standing Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":10,"pct":50},{"max":1,"r":5,"pct":60},{"max":1,"r":5,"pct":70},{"max":1,"r":1,"pct":80},{"max":1,"r":1,"pct":90},{"max":1,"r":1,"pct":100}],"note":"Max Effort Method"},{"ss":[{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lying Tricep Extension (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":10,"pct":30},{"max":1,"r":10,"pct":40},{"max":1,"r":5,"pct":50},{"max":1,"r":5,"pct":60},{"max":1,"r":5,"pct":70},{"max":1,"r":5,"pct":80},{"max":1,"r":5,"pct":90},{"max":1,"r":5,"pct":100}],"note":"Run the rack!"},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]}]},{"n":"Landmine Oblique Twist","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"pct":67.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pin Press Bench (Barbell)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"pct":67.5},{"amrap":1,"pct":70},{"amrap":1,"pct":82.5}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":4}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":4}]},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":4}]}]},{